<title>GERMANY: George-&quot;tragedy&quot; if EU distracted by EMU timetable.</title>
<headline>George-&quot;tragedy&quot; if EU distracted by EMU timetable.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Governor Eddie George said on Tuesday he saw a deep consensus within Europe regarding economic management and macroeconomic policies.</p>
<p>But George, speaking during a panel discussion at the Global 24 conference, said it would be a &quot;tragedy&quot; if nations were diverted from their pursuit of such policies by the determination to meet a timetable for the European monetary union.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
